This chapter introduces the concept of and opportunity for metal AM. AM is radically changing the aerospace industry and spawning new business opportunities in what has been a fairly small market with only a few major players. The aerospace propulsion industry is challenging and the stakes are high. Metallic components and complex assemblies must operate flawlessly in harsh environments, while simultaneously reducing mass for flight applications that are human-rated. Manufacturing of these complex components can often take several years, and quality must be exceptional. The complex designs of these high-performance components combined with long-lead-time metal alloys can make manufacturing very expensive. AM is enabling high-complexity designs with significantly reduced lead times. Cost reductions in small-batch production and reduced certification effort further justify the business case for AM propulsion systems. AM provides the ability to fabricate components from metals that are otherwise difficult to process. This chapter provides an overview of the advantages and challenges of AM, as well as some highlights of use applications across the industry, including the enabling of a new commercial space market.
