1.5. SUMMARY
Metal AM is certainly recognized to be changing the aerospace industry. Additive manufacturing is being integrated into propulsion systems for commercial aircraft, rocket engines, in-space applications, and many other advanced systems to reduce lead times and associated costs, reduce waste, eliminate supply-chain challenges for specialty manufacturing processes or obsolescence issues, and improve performance. New industries are being developed, and new supply chains, new design opportunities, new metal alloys and materials, and novel advancements in AM are being made faster than ever before. Our goal with this book is to provide an overview of the concept-to-utilization life cycle in AM for propulsion applications. Metal Additive Manufacturing for Propulsion Applications is intended as a guide for engineers, students, and new and veteran users at all levels to advance their understanding and inspire the proper use of AM for complex propulsion applications.
